Chapter: AnnotProbe

  cites Works chapter GopEdit
  cites Works chapter GopFat16
  cites Works chapter GopAhci
  cites Works chapter RepoProtocolPersist
  cites Works chapter Annotation
  cites Kernel chapter DiskFacts
  cites Foreword chapter Fat16

 Splits the gutter-mark chain: are the annotations reaching the pane at all,
 does the chapter table build, does the matcher fire. Each stage prints, so
 the failure names itself rather than being inferred from a blank gutter.

 It earned its keep on the first run. The gutter was blank and any of five
 stages could have been the reason; STAGE 4 printed the chapter as `[Name ]`
 with a trailing space against a target of `Name`, which is the CRLF on the
 medium surviving as a space through `ged-chars`, and named the defect in one
 run instead of a bisection.

 Run it against an image seeded by `annotation-mark-seed.codex`:

   build/compile.ps1 -Src docs/Probes/annotation-mark.codex
     -Out probe.cdx -Kernel seed/Codex.cdx -Log probe.log
   tools/codex-vm.exe -kernel probe.cdx -output probe.txt -mem 3072
     -headless -disk annot.img

 A correct run reads 2 annotations on the medium, 1 mark set, and the bit
 string `000000001000000` -- the second annotation targets a name that is not
 in the file and is the control for the matcher.

Section: Entry

  bits : Integer, Integer, Integer, Text -> Text
  bits (es) (i) (n) (acc) =
    if i > n then acc
    else bits es (i + 1) n (acc & show (ged-mark-get es (i - 1)))

  opening : [Console, Device.Port, Device.Block] Nothing = act
    let store = disk-load
    in let anns = repo-persist-load-all-annotations store
    in act
      print-line-uni ("STAGE 1 annotations on medium: " & show (list-length anns))
      m <- gfat-mount-esp
      if m.gm-ok == False then print-line-uni "MOUNT failed"
      else act
        let vol = m.gm-vol
        in let es = alloc-zeroed 64 64
        in let i0 = ged-init es
        in act
          got <- gfat-read-file-bulk vol "SRC/NAME.COD" (ged-buf es)
          let p = poke-32 es 8 got
          in let c = ged-reindex es
          in act
            print-line-uni ("STAGE 2 file bytes=" & show (ged-size es) & " lines=" & show (ged-count es))
            let s = ged-chap-scan es
            in act
              print-line-uni ("STAGE 3 chapters found=" & show (ged-chap-count es) & " first at line=" & show (if ged-chap-count es > 0 then ged-chap-line es 0 else 0 - 1))
              print-line-uni ("STAGE 4 chapter name at that line: [" & (if ged-chap-count es > 0 then chap-name-of es 0 else "<none>") & "]")
              print-line-uni ("STAGE 5 line 9 text: [" & ged-line-text es 8 60 & "]")
              hits <- (ged-annots-load es)
              act
                print-line-uni ("STAGE 6 marks set=" & show hits)
                print-line-uni ("STAGE 7 bits lines 1..15: " & bits es 1 15 "")
              end
            end
          end
        end
      end
    end
  end

  chap-name-of : Integer, Integer -> Text
  chap-name-of (es) (ci) =
    let line = ged-chap-line es ci
    in let full = ged-line-text es line 200
    in if text-length full > 9 then substring full 9 (text-length full - 9) else full
